{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Day 25 — Visualization with Matplotlib & seaborn\n","Objectives:\n","- Core plot types: hist, box, violin, bar, line, scatter.\n","- Aesthetics and themes.\n","- Save figures for reports."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["import seaborn as sns, matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","df = sns.load_dataset('tips')\n","sns.histplot(data=df, x='total_bill', kde=True)\n","plt.show()\n","sns.boxplot(data=df, x='day', y='tip')\n","plt.show()\n","sns.scatterplot(data=df, x='total_bill', y='tip', hue='time')\n","plt.savefig('fig_scatter.png', dpi=150)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Exercises\n","1) Recreate two plots from your EDA with improved labeling.\n","2) Export figures to `reports/figures/` with consistent style."]}]}
